course: dictionary
lesson: 5324
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so use the context to choose the right one. Look at the words around it. In «Peel back the husk and each long silky thread leads to one kernel», the husk and the silk show that a kernel is a seed inside a corn cob.
explain: In «Popcorn kernels pop when heated», a kernel is a seed grain. In «a kernel of truth», the word means the most important, central part of something. The clues tell you which meaning to use.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «the central part of truth» make sense? Almost, and the phrase is about a small true part inside a false story, so the meaning is "central" in that sense. If the swap sounds silly, try another meaning.
fact: A kernel is the soft part inside a nut, or the seed inside the hard stone of a fruit.
fact: A kernel is a whole seed of a grain such as corn (maize) or wheat.
fact: The kernel of something is its most important central part, as in «a kernel of truth».
fact: «A kernel of truth» means a small true part inside a mostly false story.
fact: Colonel is spelt c-o-l-o-n-e-l but is said "kernel".
exercise: «Heat turns the water inside each popcorn kernel to steam.» What is a kernel in this sentence? | A kind of fruit juice | A computer part | *A seed of corn | A ball of wool
exercise: Which word means the soft part inside a nut? | husk | *kernel | tassel | silk
exercise: Ella says, «The story had a kernel of truth.» What does kernel mean here? | *The small true part at the centre | A grain of wheat | A computer program | A hard shell around a nut
test: «Maize came from teosinte, whose ear held only about a dozen hard kernels.» What does kernel mean here? | The most important part of a plan | *A seed grain | A computer's core | A ball of pollen
test: In a computer, what is the kernel? | The tassel | *The core part of the operating system that controls everything else | The silk | The husk
exam: What makes a popcorn kernel burst open when it is heated? | It is ground into flour | It turns cold and hard | It is eaten raw | *Water inside turns to steam and the hard shell holds it until the kernel bursts
